'''''Ionopsidium''''' is a [[genus]] of plants in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Brassicaceae]]. It includes 9 species native to the western and central [[Mediterranean region]], from Portugal and Spain to Morocco, Algeria, Tunisia, Italy, Sicily, and Greece.<ref name = powo/>

==Species==
Nine species are accepted.<ref name = powo/>
*''[[Ionopsidium abulense]]'' {{small|(Pau) Rothm.}}
*''[[Ionopsidium acaule]]'' {{small|(Desf.) DC. ex Rchb.}}
*''[[Ionopsidium albiflorum]]'' {{small|Durieu}}
*''[[Ionopsidium aragonense]]'' {{small|(H.J.Coste & Soulié) M.Koch}}
*''[[Ionopsidium glastifolium]]'' {{small|(L.) M.Koch}}
*''[[Ionopsidium heterospermum]]'' {{small|Batt.}}
*''[[Ionopsidium megalospermum]]'' {{small|(Maire) M.Koch}}
*''[[Ionopsidium prolongoi]]'' {{small|(Boiss.) Batt.}}
*''[[Ionopsidium savianum]]'' {{small|(Caruel) Ball ex Arcang.}}

